  "sign_correction": {
    "correct_equation": "-Delta_B p = (1 - K_B) p,  -Delta_B q = (1 - K_B) q",
    "wrong_equation_step14": "-Delta_B p = (K_B - 1) p",
    "cross_gradient": "<grad p, grad q> = -K_B pq",
    "anchor_S2xS2": "-Delta(sin x) = sin x = (1 - 0)(sin x). Correct.",
    "derivation": "Besse doubly-warped Ricci for 2 one-dim fibers over 2D base; trace of horizontal equation gives gamma=K_B-1; substitution gives <grad p,grad q>/(pq) = -K_B. Checked on S^4 (K_B=1/3) and S^2xS^2 (K_B=0).",
    "crosscheck_eigenvalue": "Delta(pq) = -(1-K_B)pq - (1-K_B)pq - 2K_B pq = -2pq. Hence -Delta w = 2w. Consistent with eigenvalue equation."
  },
  "green_identity_corrected": {
    "derivation": "Green(p-eq * q): int <grad p, grad q> + int (Delta p)q = int_bdry q d_nu p. Substituting: -int K_B w - int (1-K_B)w = -int w. Boundary: -Phi_p. Hence Phi_p = int w.",
    "result": "Phi_p = Phi_q = int_Omega w dA. Total flux = 2 int w.",
    "key_consequence": "K_B cancels completely. There is NO interior weighted-curvature identity. The 'int K_B w = int w' from Step 20 was an artifact of the wrong sign in the individual equations.",
    "anchor_S2xS2": "K_B=0, int w = 4. Phi_p (p-rods) = int sin y dy [x=0] + int sin y dy [x=pi] = 2 + 2 = 4 = int w. CHECK."
  },
